Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk had
**412 reports** merged into #4471. They are not one bug. They are **three problems**, and each now has its own ticket.

<Callout>
Not "known, one fix queued". The parser fix covers 374 of the 412 reports. The other 38 need different fixes.
</Callout>

## The three problems

| Problem | Reports | Ticket |
|---|---|---|
| Shared parser reads dates month first, so day-first tenants get month and day flipped (`parser`) | **374** | [issue 1](https://github.com/rvazquezglez/what-it-shows-4471/issues/1) |
| booking-v3 form hint prints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants, who type month first (`hint`) | **33** | [issue 2](https://github.com/rvazquezglez/what-it-shows-4471/issues/2) |
| A one-day shift (timezone-like), not a month/day swap | **5** | [issue 3](https://github.com/rvazquezglez/what-it-shows-4471/issues/3) |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412. The five one-day reports (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) are listed in
`desk-notes.json`; the table below files them under `parser` because of their tenant, so it shows 379 there.

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the browser. 15 of the 33 `hint` reports were tagged `parser`.

